      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nHonor `draft_load_config` for standalone drafts on both model runners and MRV2 hidden-state extraction. These loaders previously inherited the target's load config.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Apply the existing `ipc_cache` disk fallback and MRV2 pipeline-safe loader fallback.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Focused worker suites: 19 passed after rebasing; pre-commit and diff checks passed.\r\n- Standalone GPU validation before rebasing (GB10, Qwen3-1.7B / Qwen3-0.6B, TP=PP=DP=1): baseline IPC loading failed on both runners; fixed loading succeeded with 45/51 draft tokens accepted and all 64 output tokens matching target-only generation.\r\n- Hidden-state loading, distributed PP, and explicit draft overrides remain unvalidated end to end. GPU validation was not repeated after rebasing.\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_extract_hidden_states_speculator.py tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py -q\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nReuse `get_draft_load_config()` and MRV2's `get_pp_safe_draft_load_config()`.\r\n\r\nDuplicate checks found no equivalent standalone fix; Related: [#55337](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/55337) covers EAGLE loading.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>",
